; Design record 22 section 3.7: the USB4 software connection manager's
; hosts (Phase 40). Lunar, Panther and Wildcat Lake and Barlow Ridge by
; id, AMD's Pink Sardine, Rembrandt, Phoenix, Strix, Strix Halo, Krackan
; and Krackan2 (task 46.23) and ASMedia's ASM4242 (task 45.46) named
; beside the class line, and any other USB4 host (class 0C/03/40) by the
; class line, which the id lines outrank. xhcicm.sys takes each as a USB4
; host (cm_vals.c) and runs the software connection manager on it when the
; selection of record 22 section 3.6 picks it (cm_nhi.c). XhciCmMode 0
; (off) leaves it inert, and 2 (the firmware connection manager's client
; only) never runs the software one.
%U4LnDesc%=Cm.Dev,PCI\VEN_8086&DEV_A833
%U4LnDesc%=Cm.Dev,PCI\VEN_8086&DEV_A834
